10:34:41    If the Courant column is flat, the time step is not the cause.
10:34:41    If hom peak is flat, the homogeneous reference is sound and
10:34:41    the differencing is clean, so the error belongs to the
10:34:41    interface and not to the harness.
10:34:41    If growth is negative everywhere the scheme is stable, and
10:34:41    marginal instability is excluded.
10:34:41    If the error varies smoothly through 45 and is no better at
10:34:41    54.74, the body-diagonal alignment argument does not explain
10:34:41    it. If it dips at 54.74 the alignment argument does explain
10:34:41    it, and 45 degrees is simply the worst case rather than a bug.
